  "description": "Host bridge for the two law-derived Accommodation Supplement inputs that rulespec-nz takes as inputs \"for later cross-module wiring\": the Social Security Regulations 2018 reg 17 base rate and the reg 18 non-beneficiary income cutout. Every rate is to come from an engine evaluation of a bound rulespec-nz module; this resource declares only which outputs combine, with which coefficients, under which input overrides. No bridge graph node exists yet (package G7). It ports the statutory branch (treasury_host_aligned false) of the axiom-oracles IncomeExplorer conformance harness. Under method card amendment MC11a, which is proposed (awaiting D1), it would be the one sanctioned exception to \"real Axiom runtime only\"; it needs Max's MC11 ruling. When rulespec-nz encodes regs 17 and 18 (6 Oct plan B13), this resource and the bridge graph nodes are to be deleted, and only the Accommodation Supplement branches will re-run.",
  "status": "awaiting D1 (MC11; amendment MC11a proposed)",
